{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"ama-lost-little-goat","version":1,"title":"Ama and the Lost Little Goat","ageTiers":["3-4","5-6"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"Ama lived in a small village with her family. She had a little goat named Pepe. Pepe had a white spot on his nose.","sentences":["Ama lived in a small village with her family.","She had a little goat named Pepe.","Pepe had a white spot on his nose."],"image":"sha256:8d573e8652ddab4ba50cb70ed657311f1b8fa582cde6da39cff93a07eae0b601","alt":"A smiling girl with yellow ribbons hugs a small brown goat with a white spot on its nose, in front of a mud-brick house.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:f5d11a9312112631be4dbe72ab142b1e45494acba7a952b97d10f3376e98d38c","durationMs":12347,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4981],[4981,8924],[8924,12347]],"words":[[0,311],[311,830],[830,1038],[1038,1246],[1246,1765],[1765,2491],[2491,2906],[2906,3217],[3217,4981],[4981,5292],[5292,5603],[5603,5811],[5811,6434],[6434,6849],[6849,7368],[7368,8924],[8924,9339],[9339,9650],[9650,9858],[9858,10377],[10377,10792],[10792,11000],[11000,11311],[11311,12347]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"Every morning Ama gave Pepe fresh water and green leaves. Pepe said, ‘Meh-eh-eh!’ Ama laughed.","sentences":["Every morning Ama gave Pepe fresh water and green leaves.","Pepe said, ‘Meh-eh-eh!’ Ama laughed."],"image":"sha256:217b4c0ade970fc1ee0b4be33a24df95c1aea82719b961299373c332aa20a697","alt":"Ama holds out green leaves to the goat, who stretches his neck to eat them.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:424d542e4445164c8d3537c465002c63d2808ab060e5bbe40a1d317556e03f1a","durationMs":11627,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,6423],[6423,11627]],"words":[[0,554],[554,1329],[1329,1661],[1661,2104],[2104,2547],[2547,3101],[3101,3655],[3655,3987],[3987,4541],[4541,6423],[6423,6866],[6866,7863],[7863,9856],[9856,10188],[10188,11627]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"One sunny day, Ama went to fetch water. When she came back, Pepe was gone! ‘Pepe! Pepe!’ called Ama.","sentences":["One sunny day, Ama went to fetch water.","When she came back, Pepe was gone!","‘Pepe!","Pepe!’ called Ama."],"image":"sha256:d1c7db1663bb2373ca0f64497d46c4377042704af6f8ffeae3fd940d77bf1ff4","alt":"Ama stands holding a bucket, looking at an empty post where the goat was tied. She looks worried.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:26aa2db90d0b43bd222e59602290e1071e875559ebec0046eb69ce2748529305","durationMs":12947,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4479],[4479,8566],[8566,10026],[10026,12947]],"words":[[0,292],[292,779],[779,1558],[1558,1850],[1850,2239],[2239,2434],[2434,2921],[2921,4479],[4479,4868],[4868,5160],[5160,5549],[5549,6425],[6425,6814],[6814,7106],[7106,8566],[8566,10026],[10026,11486],[11486,12070],[12070,12947]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"Ama looked by the mango tree. A hen sat there with her chicks. ‘Have you seen Pepe?’ asked Ama. ‘Cluck, cluck, not here,’ said the hen. ‘Try near the well.’","sentences":["Ama looked by the mango tree.","A hen sat there with her chicks.","‘Have you seen Pepe?’ asked Ama.","‘Cluck, cluck, not here,’ said the hen.","‘Try near the well.’"],"image":"sha256:6af18295db29d0592715e48b532ded4e37e13dfbd1b367f5aad4fd18cee96927","alt":"Under a mango tree a speckled hen and four chicks talk to Ama.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:245fe5044b4f8a5dd19eac1152f320d39f7da75611e7f343bd232f533a3a0e3e","durationMs":13355,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2402],[2402,5016],[5016,8196],[8196,11942],[11942,13355]],"words":[[0,212],[212,636],[636,777],[777,989],[989,1342],[1342,2402],[2402,2543],[2543,2755],[2755,2967],[2967,3320],[3320,3603],[3603,3815],[3815,5016],[5016,5299],[5299,5511],[5511,5794],[5794,6854],[6854,7207],[7207,8196],[8196,8903],[8903,9610],[9610,9822],[9822,10458],[10458,10741],[10741,10953],[10953,11942],[11942,12154],[12154,12437],[12437,12649],[12649,13355]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"At the well, Ama met old Grandpa Yaw. ‘Have you seen my goat?’ she asked. Grandpa Yaw smiled. ‘I heard a small voice by the big rock.’","sentences":["At the well, Ama met old Grandpa Yaw.","‘Have you seen my goat?’ she asked.","Grandpa Yaw smiled.","‘I heard a small voice by the big rock.’"],"image":"sha256:602f40174f5bf1384ee0ea35613240f9fb96a08bdb9823be56063cedea82762e","alt":"Ama speaks to a smiling elderly man with a white beard beside a village well.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:096d1b5b5125d5b653721425476d9969543f449cc8c827ae6595567a7a1f9597","durationMs":14243,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4044],[4044,8364],[8364,10845],[10845,14243]],"words":[[0,184],[184,460],[460,1287],[1287,1563],[1563,1839],[1839,2115],[2115,2758],[2758,4044],[4044,4412],[4412,4688],[4688,5056],[5056,5240],[5240,6618],[6618,6894],[6894,8364],[8364,9007],[9007,9283],[9283,10845],[10845,11029],[11029,11488],[11488,11672],[11672,12131],[12131,12590],[12590,12774],[12774,13050],[13050,13326],[13326,14243]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"Ama ran to the big rock. She stopped and listened. ‘Meh-eh-eh!’ It was Pepe! His rope was caught on a branch.","sentences":["Ama ran to the big rock.","She stopped and listened.","‘Meh-eh-eh!’ It was Pepe!","His rope was caught on a branch."],"image":"sha256:a93cc28f548d8d4b7bfce90158a50444a770eeede4f1d50db448e93b4c72257e","alt":"Behind a large rock, the little goat stands with its rope caught on a low branch, and Ama runs toward him.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:83c66448f2a84177f8d8e269e42e1eda7bf087f2886664ed2e9b982d70820707","durationMs":14747,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3266],[3266,6869],[6869,11147],[11147,14747]],"words":[[0,338],[338,676],[676,901],[901,1239],[1239,1577],[1577,3266],[3266,3604],[3604,4392],[4392,4730],[4730,6869],[6869,8895],[8895,9120],[9120,9458],[9458,11147],[11147,11485],[11485,11935],[11935,12273],[12273,12948],[12948,13173],[13173,13398],[13398,14747]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"Ama gently freed the rope. Pepe licked her hand. ‘Thank you for helping me,’ Ama told Grandpa Yaw and the hen.","sentences":["Ama gently freed the rope.","Pepe licked her hand.","‘Thank you for helping me,’ Ama told Grandpa Yaw and the hen."],"image":"sha256:e9168bff7b58038f35d57673da19762997fe3efde1931472c837e20bc6732bae","alt":"Ama unties the rope while the goat nuzzles her hand; the old man and the hen look on, smiling.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:21144293c9d82d6fc97d6241e0a619b9d5e0852ac0b672d54a70b6e14331de57","durationMs":11027,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3016],[3016,5655],[5655,11027]],"words":[[0,283],[283,848],[848,1319],[1319,1602],[1602,3016],[3016,3393],[3393,3958],[3958,4241],[4241,5655],[5655,6126],[6126,6409],[6409,6692],[6692,7352],[7352,8012],[8012,8295],[8295,8672],[8672,9332],[9332,9615],[9615,9898],[9898,10181],[10181,11027]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"That evening Ama tied Pepe’s rope to a strong post. ‘Stay close, little one,’ she whispered. Pepe closed his eyes and went to sleep. The end.","sentences":["That evening Ama tied Pepe’s rope to a strong post.","‘Stay close, little one,’ she whispered.","Pepe closed his eyes and went to sleep.","The end."],"image":"sha256:2dab8b47571d87c7e1cbc7be132e34cc62cf36a786bfc2a683ec41676906fb91","alt":"At sunset Ama strokes the sleeping goat beside a sturdy post.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:8be00b1e3addfaf80e3e18c7a12468b3802d44bac6c7c71c98dadc5e1209a1c8","durationMs":23675,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,7842],[7842,15532],[15532,21865],[21865,23675]],"words":[[0,603],[603,1659],[1659,2111],[2111,2714],[2714,3468],[3468,4071],[4071,4373],[4373,4675],[4675,5580],[5580,7842],[7842,8445],[8445,9953],[9953,10858],[10858,12064],[12064,12516],[12516,15532],[15532,16135],[16135,17040],[17040,17492],[17492,18095],[18095,18547],[18547,19150],[19150,19452],[1945